Files
-----
face_landmarker.task
    MediaPipe Face Landmarker model bundle (float16, version 1): face detector
    and the 478-point face mesh with iris landmarks. Source:
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task
    Docs: https://ai.google.dev/edge/mediapipe/solutions/vision/face_landmarker

wasm/vision_wasm_internal.js
wasm/vision_wasm_internal.wasm
    The SIMD WebAssembly runtime shipped in the @mediapipe/tasks-vision 1.1.1
    npm package (https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe). The .wasm is
    byte-identical to the package. The .js has two lines added at the top
    (`/* eslint-disable */` and a comment) so the repository's lint run skips
    vendored code; nothing else is changed. The non-SIMD
    fallback (vision_wasm_nosimd_internal.*) and the ES-module variant
    (vision_wasm_module_internal.*) are left out on purpose to keep the
    repository small; current evergreen browsers all support WebAssembly SIMD.

Refresh
-------
When the @mediapipe/tasks-vision version changes, copy
node_modules/@mediapipe/tasks-vision/wasm/vision_wasm_internal.{js,wasm} over the
files in wasm/ so the runtime matches the JavaScript bundle that lib/capture imports,
then put the two header lines back at the top of vision_wasm_internal.js.
